    "math": false,
    "text": "7.1 The pinned environment is part of the claim\n"
  },
  {
    "block": 3,
    "bbox": [
      62.30099868774414,
      176.40298461914062,
      549.3541870117188,
      187.3120880126953
    ],
    "math": false,
    "text": "The formal project names Lean leanprover/lean4:v4.34.0-rc2, with reported Lean commit 6a10ac8c\n"
  },
  {
    "block": 4,
    "bbox": [
      62.6400146484375,
      190.76498413085938,
      549.3477172851562,
      201.67408752441406
    ],
    "math": false,
    "text": "22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d. Its Lake manifest pins Mathlib at aeb72f1e9981b6d35b426b16dc\n"
  },
  {
    "block": 5,
    "bbox": [
      62.6400146484375,
      205.12698364257812,
      549.3524780273438,
      216.0360870361328
    ],
    "math": false,
    "text": "a7759be3e7ba06. The project version is 1.0.1. The archived configuration records moreLeanArgs = [\"-E\n"
  },
  {
    "block": 6,
    "bbox": [
      62.6400146484375,
      219.48898315429688,
      549.37060546875,
      244.76109313964844
    ],
    "math": false,
    "text": "\", \"warning\"]. That setting alone does not establish warning rejection. The recorded compiler controls\nidentify the behavior actually checked.\n"
  },
  {
    "block": 7,
    "bbox": [
      62.6400146484375,
      250.70401000976562,
      551.181640625,
      290.3371276855469
    ],
    "math": false,
    "text": "The preserved release deliberately omits compiled outputs and dependency caches. A fresh environ-\nment therefore needs the pinned toolchain and the dependencies named by the manifest. Rebuilding\nthe PDF guide does not need Lean. Replaying the mathematical formalization does.\n"
  },
  {
    "block": 8,
    "bbox": [
      62.6400146484375,
      296.2799987792969,
      551.1823120117188,
      335.91412353515625
    ],
    "math": false,
    "text": "Descriptive dependency branches such as master or main are not substitutes for exact manifest revi-\nsions. Updating a dependency and obtaining a successful build may be useful, but it is a new verifica-\ntion event. The original event remains tied to the recorded environment.\n"
  },
  {
    "block": 9,
    "bbox": [
      62.63999938964844,
      355.74072265625,
      409.8385925292969,
      367.49664306640625
    ],
    "math": false,
    "text": "7.2 A map gate and a namespace gate answer different questions\n"
